{"version":"6.9","hitCount":1,"request":{"queryString":"EXT_ID:1059131 AND SRC:MED","internalQuery":"EXT_ID:1059131 AND SRC:MED","resultType":"CORE","cursorMark":"*","pageSize":25,"sort":"","synonym":false},"resultList":{"result":[{"id":"1059131","source":"MED","pmid":"1059131","pmcid":"PMC433011","fullTextIdList":{"fullTextId":["PMC433011"]},"doi":"10.1073/pnas.72.9.3448","title":"Substrate specificity of the cyclic AMP-dependent protein kinase.","authorString":"Kemp BE, Bylund DB, Huang TS, Krebs EG.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"Kemp BE","lastName":"Kemp","firstName":"B E","initials":"BE","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-6735-5082"}},{"fullName":"Bylund DB","lastName":"Bylund","firstName":"D B","initials":"DB"},{"fullName":"Huang TS","lastName":"Huang","firstName":"T S","initials":"TS"},{"fullName":"Krebs EG","lastName":"Krebs","firstName":"E G","initials":"EG"}]},"authorIdList":{"authorId":[{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-6735-5082"}]},"dataLinksTagsList":{"dataLinkstag":["related_data"]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"9","volume":"72","journalIssueId":409195,"dateOfPublication":"1975 Sep","monthOfPublication":9,"yearOfPublication":1975,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"Proc Natl Acad Sci U S A","title":"Proceedings of the National Academy of Sciences of the United States of America","essn":"1091-6490","issn":"0027-8424","isoabbreviation":"Proc Natl Acad Sci U S A","nlmid":"7505876"},"printPublicationDate":"1975-09-01"},"pubYear":"1975","pageInfo":"3448-3452","abstractText":"The protein substrate specificity of the catalytic subunit of rabbit skeletal muscle cyclic AMP-dependent protein kinase (EC 2.7.1.37; ATP:protein phosphotransferase) has been studied using genetic variants of beta casein. It was found that beta casein-B was phosphorylated at a much greater rate than beta caseins A1, A2, A3, or C. The enhanced phosphorylation of beta casein-B, as compared with the most common variant A2, was attributed to an arginine substitution for a serine at position 122, which caused a nearby residue, serine 124, to become a phosphorylation site for the protein kinase. These results further support the concept that the local primary structure is important in specificity and that arginine may be a specific determinant common to all the local phosphorylation site sequences recognized by the cyclic AMP-dependent protein kinase.","publicationStatus":"ppublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Print","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["Research Support, U.S. Gov't, P.H.S.","research-article","Journal Article"]},"meshHeadingList":{"meshHeading":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Muscles","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"EN","qualifierName":"enzymology"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Animals"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Rabbits"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Protein Kinases","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Caseins","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Amino Acid Sequence"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Structure-Activity Relationship"}]},"chemicalList":{"chemical":[{"name":"Caseins","registryNumber":"0"},{"name":"Protein Kinases","registryNumber":"EC 2.7.-"}]},"subsetList":{"subset":[{"code":"IM","name":"Index Medicus"}]},"fullTextUrlList":{"fullTextUrl":[{"availability":"Free","availabilityCode":"F","documentStyle":"pdf","site":"Unpaywall","url":"https://europepmc.org/articles/pmc433011?pdf=render"},{"availability":"Subscription required","availabilityCode":"S","documentStyle":"doi","site":"DOI","url":"https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.72.9.3448"},{"availability":"Free","availabilityCode":"F","documentStyle":"html","site":"Europe_PMC","url":"https://europepmc.org/articles/PMC433011"},{"availability":"Free","availabilityC